        "description": "<p>A block editor that supports editing tables in Markdown notation.</p>\n<p>You can edit Markdown tables by adding, deleting, moving columns and rows, aligning text, and shaping.<br />\nPlease see here for specific operations.</p>\n<p>This is a port of the VSCode extension &#8220;MdTableEditor&#8221; to the block editor.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=clover.md-table-editor\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=clover.md-table-editor</a></p>\n<p>Please see here for specific operations.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/denki-kurage/md-table-editor-with-block-editor/blob/main/src/kurage/document/readme.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://github.com/denki-kurage/md-table-editor-with-block-editor/blob/main/src/kurage/document/readme.md</a></p>\n<p>for developers.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/denki-kurage/md-table-editor-with-block-editor\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://github.com/denki-kurage/md-table-editor-with-block-editor</a></p>\n<p>Venders</p>\n<p>vender-licenses.md</p>\n<h3>Arbitrary section</h3>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Go to the admin screen</li>\n<li>Open the &#8220;Plugins&#8221; item and click &#8220;Add New Plugin&#8221;</li>\n<li>Enter &#8220;MdTableEditor&#8221; in the search box.</li>\n<li>Find &#8220;MdTableEditor with WordPress Block Editor&#8221; and click &#8220;Install&#8221;</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='a%20question%20that%20someone%20might%20have'>\nA question that someone might have\n</h4>\n<p></p>\n<dt id='what%20about%20foo%20bar%3F'>\nWhat about foo bar?\n</h4>\n<p></p>\n\n",
